WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.295
Let's make Pressed-flower bookmarks.

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:07.938
Press flowers until dry, arrange them on card, and seal the design under clear

3
00:00:07.938 --> 00:00:08.690
adhesive film.

4
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.610
The drying stage takes several days.

5
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.070
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.180
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.805
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:20.185 --> 00:00:25.381
An adult identifies suitable plants, prepares the card and film, and checks flowers are

9
00:00:25.381 --> 00:00:26.865
fully dry before sealing.

10
00:00:27.245 --> 00:00:29.830
Never press unknown or irritating plants.

11
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:32.523
Step 1.

12
00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:35.313
Arrange flowers for pressing.

13
00:00:35.693 --> 00:00:38.863
Place two sheets of absorbent paper inside the book.

14
00:00:39.243 --> 00:00:44.328
Lay petals and small flowers in one layer, leaving a finger-width between pieces.

15
00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:46.723
Avoid thick flower centres.

16
00:00:47.103 --> 00:00:48.483
Grown-up help.

17
00:00:48.863 --> 00:00:51.598
Check the plant pieces and choose a suitable book.

18
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.180
Step 2.

19
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.765
Press and wait.

20
00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:59.230
Cover with two more sheets of paper and close the book.

21
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.370
Put it in a dry place under another heavy book.

22
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:07.735
Check after 7 days; leave longer if pieces feel cool, soft or damp.

23
00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:09.495
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:09.875 --> 00:01:14.385
Help change damp paper and check for mould; discard spoiled pieces.

25
00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.179
Step 3.

26
00:01:17.559 --> 00:01:19.024
Plan the bookmark.

27
00:01:19.404 --> 00:01:24.619
On the 5 by 15 centimetres card, arrange two or three fully dry pieces.

28
00:01:24.999 --> 00:01:27.399
Leave a 1 centimetres clear border.

29
00:01:27.779 --> 00:01:32.719
Try a single flower, a border or a petal pattern before fixing the design.

30
00:01:33.099 --> 00:01:34.479
Grown-up help.

31
00:01:34.859 --> 00:01:36.934
Prepare the card rectangle.

32
00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:39.484
Step 4.

33
00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:41.114
Seal the front.

34
00:01:41.494 --> 00:01:44.299
An adult peels the backing from one film piece.

35
00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:48.879
Lower its sticky side onto the front of the card from one short edge

36
00:01:48.879 --> 00:01:51.279
to the other, smoothing gently over the flowers.

37
00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:54.294
Fold the extra film around the edges.

38
00:01:54.674 --> 00:01:56.054
Grown-up help.

39
00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.604
Prepare and position the film.

40
00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:01.176
Step 5.

41
00:02:01.556 --> 00:02:03.221
Seal the back and finish.

42
00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.141
Apply the second film piece to the back.

43
00:02:06.521 --> 00:02:09.736
Fold its edges around to the front and smooth them flat.

44
00:02:10.116 --> 00:02:12.516
An adult trims any sticky overhang.

45
00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:16.246
Check the bookmark has smooth edges before putting it in a book.

46
00:02:16.626 --> 00:02:18.006
Grown-up help.

47
00:02:18.386 --> 00:02:21.216
Trim film and check for exposed adhesive.

48
00:02:22.668 --> 00:02:25.583
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

49
00:02:25.963 --> 00:02:29.513
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

50
00:02:29.893 --> 00:02:31.913
Your creation can look different.

51
00:02:32.293 --> 00:02:38.233
Film and coated card are mixed materials; follow local disposal rules instead of composting

52
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:38.658
them.

53
00:02:39.038 --> 00:02:43.233
Keep dry and out of strong sunlight; natural colours may fade.

54
00:02:43.613 --> 00:02:44.603
Well done.

55
00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:47.413
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

